/* book Worked example: Q: A four-cylinder petrol engine needs 45 N·m of cranking torque at 200 rpm. Calculate the cranking power and the angular speed.
   1. Given: T = 45 N·m, N = 200 rpm.
   2. Convert speed: ω = 2πN ÷ 60 = 2π × 200 ÷ 60 = 20.94 rad/s.
   3. Find power: P = Tω = 45 N·m × 20.94 rad/s = 942.5 W, taken as 942 W.
   4. In kilowatts: P = 942.5 ÷ 1000 = 0.942 kW.
   Answer: The cranking power is 942 W, or about 0.942 kW, at an angular speed of 20.94 rad/s. */
