/* book exam traps: The ignition switch does not carry starter current. It works a relay or solenoid; a switch that carried 250 A would weld its contacts in weeks. | Pull-in and hold-in coils are not both active all the time. Once the main contacts close they short the pull-in coil; only the hold-in coil keeps the plunger in. | Terminal 30 is battery positive (unswitched) and terminal 50 is the control line. Swapping them sends cranking current through the key switch. | The pinion must disengage after the engine fires. Without a working overrunning clutch or return spring, the engine spins the starter and destroys it. */
