/* book exam traps: Domain mix-up: ignition secondary is kilovolts; EV traction is hundreds of volts; the 12 V bus is neither. | Primary versus secondary: the coil primary is a low-voltage winding; the secondary is the high-voltage winding. | Fuse job: a fuse limits current to protect wiring; it does not set or limit spark voltage. | Voltage drop: a high-resistance wire or ground drops volts only when current flows; an open circuit can show full voltage with no current. | EV pre-charge: the pre-charge resistor is not the main contactor; it limits capacitor inrush before the main contactor closes. */
